1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT lejohnson_64   lejohnson_64@yahoo.com
2 CONT
2 CONT 4/20/2016
2 CONT To: Terjeroed Hansen
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Mr. Terjeroed Hansen, I don’t know if you remember me, my name is Larry Johnson, from United States of America. I was inquiring about Hans Neilsen family.  I have learned from a family member, that when my 2x Great Grandmothe
2 CONC r, Johanne Hansdatter Passed away, in Onalaska, LaCrosse, Wisconsin, in 1886, her daughter,  my Great Grandmother Martha Henrietta Vaastad, was raised by a family by the name of Poulsen and that she was raised by an aunt of my 2nd
2 CONC  great grandmother, Johanne Hansdatter.  I have researched the information they had provided.  It turns out that the aunt was Gunhild Olsdatter, born: 03 May 1824, daughter of Ole Andersen and Johanne Christiansdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild Olsdatter married Svend Hansen, 22 September1849, they immigrated to America about 1850.  Svend Hansen passed away: 23 May 1863, in Holmen, Lacrosse, Wisconsin, USA.  Gunhild Olsdatter remarried to, Halvor Poulsen: 24 July
2 CONC  1867, Gunhild Olsdatter, father Ole Andersen and mother Johanne Christiansdatter.  Gunhild Olsdatter died: 19 June 1902, in Holmen, Lacrosse, Wiscosin, USA.  This also confirms that I have the correct Hans Neilsen family.
2 CONT
2 CONT I was wondering if you might know of any other ancesters that might have immigrated to America?  This is so exciting, that we are able to connect like this, finding relatives in another country, where my family comes from.  Are yo
2 CONC u a direct descendant of Hans Neilsen?
2 CONT
2 CONT I was able to locate my Great Grandmothers birth and baptism record,  she was baptized in, Paulus Kirke, Christiania, Oslo, Norway, born:  22 September, 1882, baptized: 06 May, 1883.  Hope to hear from you soon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Your American Family,
2 CONT
2 CONT Larry Johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT Marta Henrietta Vaastad aka Martha Henrietta Vostad Born: 22 September 1882, in Chrisiania, Oslo, Norway, baptized 06 May 1883 in Paulus Kirke Oslo, Norway, she died 01 June 1987 in Bode, Iowa, USA.  Martha came to America with he
2 CONC r mother and older brother, they had departed from Christiania, Norway and Copenhegen Denmark, they arrived in New York, New York, United States of America 31 May 1884, the name of the ship was Hekla, not quite sure when her fathe
2 CONC r, Peder Andreasen Vaastad emigrated, perhaps you might be able to help me locate when he emigrated to America? Martha is the daughter of Peder Andreasen Vaastad and Johanne Hansdatter
