1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Einar Valdthjov von Krogh Beyer''' (1870-1960) Norwegian consul in Seattle, 1930-1945
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Fakta====
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born in Bergen 27th Aug 1870
2 CONT * Batisted in Bergen 25th Sep 1870
2 CONT * Comfirmed his religion in Bergen 3rd Oct 1866
2 CONT * Moved from Hamburg, Germany to Seattle in 1914
2 CONT * Norwegian consul in Seattle 1930-1945
2 CONT * Died in Seattle 7th Dec 1960
2 CONT * Furnial and cremation in Seattle 9th Dec 1960 at the Adams Forkner chapel
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fra boken: The saga of Haakon Beyer Friele '''Chapter II - Einar Beyer'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Einar Beyer was born in Bergen in 1871 and passed away in Seattle in 1961, the brother of Haakon's mother. He never married and took a spesial interest in the three fatherless sons of his sister. He lived in Hamburg, Germany for m
2 CONC any years, employed by a firm in the fish business and the three boys spent vacation periods with him in Hamburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to San Francisco on his first trip to the United States in 1906 arriving a few days after the great earthquake and fire in that city, for the purpose of purchasing mild-cured salmon caught and paced on the Sacramento River
2 CONC , for his company in Germany. He later decided to establish an American company and operate salmon canneries in Southeastern Alaska under the name of Southern Alaska Canning Company. This company failed during the 1921 depression 
2 CONC and he later formed Northern Products Company, purchasing mildcured salmon for export and sale in the United States. He resided in Seattle for many years and in later years lived in New Yourk but still maintained his office in Sea
2 CONC ttle. He was Norwegian Consul in Seattle and became a prominent figure in the Norwegian colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Uncle Einar took a spesial interest in his nephew, Haakon, and invited him to Seattle in the fall of 1916 for the purpose of training him for a career in the fishing industry in Alaska.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Folketellinger====
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1875 [http://digitalarkivet.no/cgi-win/WebCens.exe?slag=visbase&sidenr=2&filnamn=f71301&gardpostnr=34850&merk=34850#ovre Einar Beyer]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Kirkebøker====
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fødte og døpte menn 1870, Bergen fylke, Korskirken, Ministerialbok nr. B 5 (1866-1871), side 101. Permanent sidelenke: [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=1963&idx_id=1963&idx_listetype=dp&idx_kjonn=m&uid=ny&idx_s
2 CONC ide=-98 Einar Valdthjov von Krogh Beyer] 25 SEP 1870 - Bergen
2 CONT
2 CONT * Konfirmerte menn 1886, Bergen fylke, Domkirken, Ministerialbok nr. C 5 (1880-1898), side 68. Permanent sidelenke: [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=7108&idx_id=7108&uid=ny&idx_side=-69 Einar Valdthjov von Krogh 
2 CONC Beyer] 3 OCT 1886 - Bergen
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gravlagt i Seattle fra The Adam Forkner Chapel 9. desember 1960
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fra avisen Seattle Times, 8. desember 1960.
2 CONT '''Last Rites Set For Einar Beyer Of Bellevue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Einar Beyer, 90, of 9921 S. E. 16th St., Bellevue, will be held at 3 o'clock tomorrow in the Adams Forkner chapel. Cremation will follow. He was Norwegian consul here from 1930 to 1945. Mr. Beyer died in a nur
2 CONC sing home Tuesday. Born in Norway, he came to Seattle in 1914. Until 1957 he owned the Northern Products Corp, a wholesale firm. Mr. Beyer was a member of the Sons of Norway and a founder of the Norse Home. Survivors include a sis
2 CONC ter, Mrs. Dagny Friele, in Norway.
