1 NAME Anna /Andersdatter Vaksdal/
2 GIVN Anna
2 SURN Andersdatter Vaksdal
2 _MARNM Hustad
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 JUL 1861
2 ADDR
3 STAE Hordaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 BAPM
2 DATE 11 AUG 1861
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JAN 1943
2 ADDR
3 CITY Madison
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE 25 JAN 1943
2 ADDR
3 STAE Dane
3 CTRY Wisconsin
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dåp; [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070221680066 Haus sokneprestembete, SAB/A-75601/H/Haa: Ministerialbok nr. A 17, 1858-1870, s. 67]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Wisconsin State Journal, Saturday, Jan 23, 1943''
2 CONT '''Mrs. Anna B. Hustad''', 81, a native of Norway, died Friday at her residence, 2444 E. Johnson st., after a long illness.
2 CONT She had lived in Madison 28 years and was the widow of Ole Hustad.
2 CONT Survivors are three daughters, Mrs. Mabel Sunhus, Mt. Horeb; Mrs. Albert Daley, Daleyville, and Mrs. S. A. Hannes, Madison; two sons, Edwin, New Glarus, and Olen, Mt. Horeb; a sister, Mrs. Andrena Engen, New Glarus; 26 grandchildr
2 CONC en, and seven great grandchildren.
2 CONT Private funeral services will be held at the home at 12:30 p.m. Monday and church services will be at 1 p.m. at Trinity Lutheran church. Rev. J. M. Walstead will officiate, and burial will be in Primrose cemetery.
2 CONT The body is at the Gunderson funeral home.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54346856/anna-b-hustad Find a grave]
