1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He left Norway when he was 25 (1892) and went to Crookston, Minn; then to Oldham, S.D. and then Bryant, S.D. He had a saloon. In Hayti, SD he had a store and restaurant with a pool hall. He kept a summer cottage at
2 CONC  Lake Norden near Hayti and had boats. In the summer the Lars Holm family and Anna Hanson family vacationed. Thelma Lindsey (Bertha Arne and Lars Holm's daughter, remembered what a wonderful time they had when they were little. Al
2 CONC l the children loved him.) After his father died in 1912, Ole went back to Norway for 2 months, enjoying visiting his family home and relatives. While there he helped build a new home for his sister Johanna. He got back to the U.S
2 CONC . just before the war --in 1914.
