1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Find a Grave: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110379789/john-j-haugen<br/>
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT Funeral services were held at Ness Lutheran Church Monday for John J. Haugen, 37, who died July 16 following surgery in a Fargo hospital.
2 CONT John Justin Haugen was born January 31, 1917 to Mr. and Mrs. Iver Haugen of Hannaford. He attended school in Greenfield Township, was baptized and confirmed in the Union Church. At the time of his marriage he transferred to Ness, 
2 CONC where he held the office of trustee.
2 CONT In 1942 he entered the armed forces and served 3 ½ years, part of the time overseas in the Philippines and was awarded the Bronze Star medal for bravery in action.
2 CONT He married Esther Sola September 22, 1946. Two sons were born to them, Elliott John and Kent Joel.
2 CONT Surviving besides his wife, sons and parents are two sisters, Mrs. Lars Mikkelson, Hawley, Minn., and Mrs. Eldren Haugen, Hannaford; two brothers, Carl L. J. Haugen of Dazey and Howard of Fargo.
2 CONT Rev. E. O. Lee of Fargo officiated at the funeral, assisted by Kenneth Roufs, Blabon, student pastor serving the parish. Military rites were conducted at the grave by members of the Cooperstown American Legion.
2 CONT Pallbearers were Alvin Swenson, Roger Lunde and Edward Johnson of Finley, Ingvard and Maynard Haugen of Hannaford, and Oscar Kaastad, Kenmare.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, July 22, 1954.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT T SGT HQ CO 383 INF REGT WORLD WAR II BSM
