1 NOTE {geni:about_me} INGVARD HAUGEN: Newspaper Obituary and Death Notice
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Forks Herald (ND) - March 21, 1988
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased Name: INGVARD HAUGEN
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ingvard Haugen 68, Hannaford, died Friday, March 18, 1988, in Griggs County Hospital, Cooperstown, N.D. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 2 p.m. Tuesday in Union Lutheran Church, rural Hannaford. Visitation will be from 10 a.m. to 9 p.m. today, with an 8 p.m. prayer service in Quam-Plaisted-Cushman Funeral Home, Cooperstown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingvard Haugen was born April 22, 1919, in Greenfield Township of Griggs County, the son of Magnus and Malena Haugen. On June 3, 1942, he married Ruth Syvertson near Hannaford. They farmed near there. He was a charter member of th
2 CONC e Western Minnesota Steam Threshers Association and of the Central North Dakota Steam Threshers Association. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors are his wife, a daughter, Lois Johnson, Cooperstown; sons, Ralph, Hannaford, Roland, Grand Forks, and Marvin, Casselton, N.D.; 10 grandchildren; a brother, Maynard, Hannaford; and siters, Inez (Mrs. Oscar) Stockeland, Ha
2 CONC nnaford; Lorain Hagelstrom, Fort Lupton, Calif., and Hazel Hobert, Sun City, Calif. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edition: FINAL Page: 5A Copyright (c) 1988 Grand Forks Herald
