1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maynard Haugen: Newspaper Obituary and Death Notice
2 CONT
2 CONT Valley City Times-Record (ND) - August 4, 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased Name: maynard haugen
2 CONT
2 CONT  Maynard J. Haugen, 89, of Hannaford, N. D., passed away Aug. 2, 2010, in Sanford Health in Fargo, N. D. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maynard was born Aug. 8, 1920, in Greenview Township Griggs Co., N. D., (near Hannaford) the son of Magnus and Malena (Lee) Haugen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended country school in there. He served in the US Air Force from 1942 to 1946 as a baker.  Upon military discharge, he returned home to work on the family farm with his father until his death.  He married Margaret Grage on 
2 CONC June 12, 1956, in Hillsboro, N. D. To this union three sons where born. The couple farmed in the Hannaford area their entire married life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maynard served many years on the Union Lutheran Church council where he was a lifetime member. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other boards Maynard served on included C. N. D. S. TR at New Rockford, N. D., Griggs & Nelson Mutual Ins., Karnak Grain, lifetime member of the Mervin J. Armstrong American Legion Post #113, William A. Armstrong VFW Post #3379. F
2 CONC or a number of years he played guitar with the "Neighbors." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maynard is survived by his wife of 54 years, Margaret, of Hannaford, N. D.; two sons, Mark (Vicki) Haugen, Hannaford,, Steven, Wahpeton, N. D.; two sisters, Hazel Hobert, Sun City, Calif., Lorraine Hagelstrom, Cooperstown, N. D., 
2 CONC five grandchildren, Lindsey, Magen, and Trevor Haugen, Jacob and Justin Ruediger. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, a son John; and infant daughter; two brothers, Ingvard Haugen, Gordon Gullickson; and a sister Inez Stockeland Blessed be the memory of a kind, loving and generous man. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Friday, Aug. 6, 2010, at 10:30 a.m. in the Union Lutheran Church, rural Hannaford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held Thursday from 5 until 7 p.m. in the church and one hour before services in the church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A prayer service will be held Thursday at 7 p.m. in the church. Interment will be in the Union Cemetery, rural Hannaford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: 6 Copyright 2010, Valley City Times-Record, All Rights Reserved.
