1 CONT Research of Leila Mikkelson Preston regarding Fylingsli (translated from the Vaksdal Bygdebok, Band III published in 1965) via email dated January 5, 2002, to Laureen Mikkelson Hayes:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1886 deeded to Johannes Olsson. He owned the other part of Fyllingslid and so now the farm was worked as one.  Johannes and wife Ingeborg lived here     until 1917. Then they moved to  Veo.
1 CONT Children:  Ola b. 1873 d. 1877 in a landslide.
1 CONT Anders b. 1879 lived at Odda     married to Lina H. Vik.
1 CONT Ola b. 1883 d. 1940;
1 CONT Nils b. 1885;
1 CONT Gunnhild b. 1887 married to Ivar Johannesson Fylingslid(your grandparents) from Fyllehaugen - settled in the USA;
1 CONT Karl b. 1889 d. 1891.
1 CONT Kari b. 1891 d. 1917 married to Nikolai Olsson Kåsstad lived USA (they were cousins);
1 CONT Malene b. 1894 married to Magnus Haugen (he was a descendent from fyllehaugen).
0 @N6000000001713190341@ NOTE Research of Leila Mikkelson Preston via email dated December 11, 2001, to Lolly Mikkelson Hayes:
1 CONT
1 CONT Iver's wife Gunhild was born and grew up on the farm just below the Fyllehaugen farm on the side of the mountain.  So I figure that Iver knew Gunhild before he emmigrated to No. Dakota.  Malena is the mother of Inez Huagen Stockla
1 CONC nd in Hannaford.  As a kid I never knew that Malena and Iver's wife were sisters.  That made Lolly's mother double relation to Inez's family too.  We have pictures of both the Fyllingsli and the Fyllehaugen farms.  It was a beauti
1 CONC ful place, but one can see why they could not make a living there.
0 @N6000000001713190353@ NOTE Immigration record,
1 CONT Bergen  No. 1916; Date  1909  Juni  26; Name:  Kari  Johannesdtr Fyllingslid;  female  ug; Occupation  Tjenestepike;  Birthyear: 1891; Age 18; Birthplace StamnesBruvik; Residence Stamnes Bruvik; Destination  Amk Hannaford No Dak; 
1 CONC  Ticket Penge; Reason  a (bedre livsvilkaar); Desired occupation  Tjeneste;   Line  Canadian Pacific
1 CONT
1 CONT Family History of Magnus and Malena Haugen:
1 CONT Malena Lee came to America from Stamnes, Norway, at age of 17.  She and her sister, Gunhild (Mrs. Iver Haugen) came together to see their sister, Carrie (Mrs. Nick Kaastad) who came earlier.  Carrie died of the flu in 1918, leavin
1 CONC g two small children, Inga and Oscar, which Magnes and Malena cared for.  Malena did housework and since she only spoke Norwegian, it wasn't always easy.  She learned quickly the English language and read and talked well, but didn
1 CONC 't write it.
